{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:98612","published":"2026-11-13T12:06:37.188502Z","modified":"2026-11-13T12:45:11.280393922Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-102266","CVE-2026-102267","CVE-2026-102268","CVE-2026-102271","CVE-2026-102272"],"summary":"Critical: fence-agents security update","details":"The fence-agents packages provide a collection of scripts for handling remote power management for cluster devices. They allow failed or unreachable nodes to be forcibly restarted and removed from the cluster. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* pyjwt: pyjwt: Authentication bypass via empty HMAC key acceptance (CVE-2026-102266)\n\n* pyjwt: PyJWT: Authentication bypass via improper public key validation (CVE-2026-102268)\n\n* pyjwt: PyJWT: Authentication bypass via acceptance of DER public keys as HMAC secrets (CVE-2026-102271)\n\n* pyjwt: pyjwt: Verification key substitution via unvalidated JWKS redirects (CVE-2026-102267)\n\n* pyjwt: pyjwt: Token forgery via improper Unicode byte-order mark handling (CVE-2026-102272)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"fence-agents-aliyun","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/fence-agents-aliyun?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.16.0-34.el10_3.1"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:98612.json"}},{"package":{"name":"fence-virtd-multicast-debuginfo","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/fence-virtd-multicast-debuginfo?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.16.0-34.el10_3.1"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.co